    "title": "📑 Session 11 — BRUSHES — Brush libraries; Creating own brushes; Pattern brushes|||📑 Buổi 11 — BRUSHES — Brush libraries; Creating own brushes; Pattern brushes",
    "slug": "dtg102-flm-b011",
    "type": "DOCUMENT",
    "isFreePreview": false,
    "description": "Buổi 11 theo syllabus FLM · 4 slide.",
    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">DTG102 · Chapter 2 · Session 11</span>\n<h2>Session 11 — BRUSHES — Brush libraries; Creating own brushes; Pattern brushes</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13371 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">DTG102 · Chương 2 · Buổi 11</span>\n<h2>Buổi 11 — BRUSHES — Brush libraries; Creating own brushes; Pattern brushes</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13371 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">4</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">4</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>BRUSHES — Brush libraries; Creating own brushes; Pattern brushes</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>📑 School slides — Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives (4 slides)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">matched by the session number in the deck name. File: Session 11_DTG102_Course objectives.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>📑 Slide của trường — Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives (4 slide)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">ghép theo số buổi ghi trong tên deck. Tệp: Session 11_DTG102_Course objectives.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d11/001.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 1: Brush up on Adobe Illustrator brushesBrushes are one of the most essential tools in the graphic designer toolbox. Adobe has…\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 1/4</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Brush up on Adobe Illustrator brushesBrushes are one of the most essential tools in the graphic designer toolbox. Adobe has tons of creative Illustrator brushes and different brush sizes and brush shapes available to create your digital designs.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d11/002.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 2: BRUSHES\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 2/4</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>BRUSHES<br>Start by opening the Brushes panel (Window &gt; Brushes).  There might be some default brushes in there, but you also may notice some custom brushes.<br>Using &amp; Editing Brushes<br>To use brushes, select a path (or draw a new one) and click on the instance of the brush in the Brushes panel.  That brush will then be applied to the path. The size of the brush can be changed by adjusting the size of the stroke.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d11/003.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 3: Transferring Brushes Between Files\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 3/4</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Transferring Brushes Between Files<br>If you have some brushes that you want to transfer between files, the quick and dirty method is via copy and paste. Select an instance of the brush that you want and choose Edit &gt; Copy (cmd/ctrl + C).  Navigate to the file where you want to use the brush, and Edit &gt; Paste (cmd/ctrl + V).  Once the brush is pasted anywhere in the document, you will notice that an instance of it has been added to the Brushes panel.  Even if you delete the brush instance from the artboard, it will remain in the Brushes panel within this particular document unless you manually delete it.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d11/004.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 4: Loading Brushes in Files\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 11 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 4/4</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Loading Brushes in Files<br>Instead of copying and pasting, you can also load brushes into your Illustrator workspace.  Click the drop down menu on the Brushes panel and choose Open Brush Library &gt; Other Library…  You will then browse out the saved brush file on your computer.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
