    "description": "Buổi 48 theo syllabus FLM · 6 slide.",
    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">DTG102 · Chapter 4 · Session 48</span>\n<h2>Session 48 — WORKING WITH PARAGRAPH — Format paragraph with Paragraph Panel; Text Thread; Text into frame/shape; Text wrap; Dropcap</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13371 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">DTG102 · Chương 4 · Buổi 48</span>\n<h2>Buổi 48 — WORKING WITH PARAGRAPH — Format paragraph with Paragraph Panel; Text Thread; Text into frame/shape; Text wrap; Dropcap</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13371 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">6</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1, CLO4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">6</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>WORKING WITH PARAGRAPH — Format paragraph with Paragraph Panel; Text Thread; Text into frame/shape; Text wrap; Dropcap</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>📑 School slides — Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives (6 slides)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">matched by the session number in the deck name. File: Session 48_DTG102_Course objectives.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>📑 Slide của trường — Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives (6 slide)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">ghép theo số buổi ghi trong tên deck. Tệp: Session 48_DTG102_Course objectives.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d24/001.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 1: Adobe InDesign\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 1/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Adobe InDesign<br>WORKING WITH PARAGRAPH</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d24/002.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 2: ADJUST PARAGRAPH SPACING\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 2/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>ADJUST PARAGRAPH SPACING<br>You can control the amount of space between paragraphs. If a paragraph begins at the top of a column or frame, InDesign does not honor the Space Before value. In such a case, you can increase the leading of the first line of the paragraph or increase the top inset of the text frame in InDesign.<br>Select text.<br>In the Paragraph panel or the Control panel, adjust the appropriate values for Space Before       , Space After      , and Space Between Paragraphs Having Same Style     .<br>2<br>FPT UNIVERSITY, GRAPHIC DESIGN<br>DIGITAL TOOL 2D</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d24/003.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 3: USE DROP CAP\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 3/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>USE DROP CAP<br>With the Type tool      selected, click in the paragraph where you want the drop cap to appear.<br>In the Paragraph panel or Control panel, type a number for Drop Cap Number Of Lines     to indicate the number of lines you want the drop cap to occupy.<br>For Drop Cap One Or More Characters     , type the number of drop cap characters you want.<br>To apply a character style to the drop cap character, choose Drop Caps And Nested Styles from the Paragraph panel menu, and then choose the character style you created.<br>3<br>FPT UNIVERSITY, GRAPHIC DESIGN<br>DIGITAL TOOL 2D</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d24/004.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 4: REMOVE DROP CAP\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 4/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>REMOVE DROP CAP<br>4<br>FPT UNIVERSITY, GRAPHIC DESIGN<br>DIGITAL TOOL 2D<br>Remove a drop cap<br>With the Type tool       selected, click in the paragraph where the drop cap appears.<br>In the Paragraph panel or Control panel, type 0 for Drop Cap Number Of Lines or Drop Cap Number Of Characters.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d24/005.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 5: ADD RULES\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 5/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>ADD RULES<br>Rules are paragraph attributes that move and are resized along with the paragraph on the page. If you’re using a rule with headings in your document, you may want to make the rule part of a paragraph style definition. The width of the rule is determined by the column width.<br>The offset for a rule above a paragraph is measured from the baseline of the top line of text to the bottom of the rule. The offset for a rule below a paragraph is measured from the baseline of the last line of text to the top of the rule.<br>5<br>FPT UNIVERSITY, GRAPHIC DESIGN<br>DIGITAL TOOL 2D</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DTG102/flm1/d24/006.webp\" alt=\"DTG102 · Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 6: CREATE HANGING PUNCTUATION\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"990\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Session 48 DTG102 Course objectives · slide 6/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>CREATE HANGING PUNCTUATION<br>Punctuation marks and letters such as “W” can make the left or right edges of a column appear to be misaligned. Optical Margin Alignment controls whether punctuation marks (such as periods, commas, quotation marks, and dashes) and edges of letters (such as W and A) hang outside the text margins, so that the type looks aligned.<br>6<br>FPT UNIVERSITY, GRAPHIC DESIGN<br>DIGITAL TOOL 2D<br>Select a text frame, or click anywhere in the story.<br>Choose Type &gt; Story.<br>Select Optical Margin Alignment.<br>Select a font size to set the appropriate amount of overhang for the size of type in your story. For optimal results, use the same size as the text.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
